; Zone Caps: Zone's own pixel capitals, drawn on this grid by hand.
;
; Built into ZoneCaps.woff2 and ZoneCaps.ttf by scripts/build-zone-caps.py.
; Never trace a screenshot: every block below was drawn from the spec in
; docs/design/surfaces/zone/REFINEMENT.md, section 2a.
;
; The spec: capitals only. A glyph is 6 art px of ink and 1 of gap (M, W
; and the wide ligatures 8 + 1; I 2 + 1; space 4). The cap is 10 art px.
; Strokes are 2 px. Diagonals are 1:1 stairs. Round letters (O C G Q S D U
; 0 6 8 9, and the bowls of B P R and the digits that curve) lose one pixel
; on each outer corner: a 45 degree notch, Zone's own signature, never a
; rounded corner. Accents stand in 3 px of headroom above the cap: 2 rows of
; mark over a 1-px gap. The digits are all 7 wide, so they are tabular.
;
; The format:
;
;   glyph U+0041          a character, by code point
;   mark grave            an accent, used by compose lines below
;   top=N                 the block's first row stands N px above the
;                         baseline (default 10: the first row is the cap's
;                         top row; marks default to 13)
;   advance=N             the advance width in art px (default: the ink's
;                         width plus the 1-px gap)
;   compose U+00C0 A grave        a capital as a base glyph and a mark,
;   compose U+0130 I dotabove dx=-1   centred over the base unless dx says
;
; '#' is ink, '.' is paper. One art px is 100 font units; the em is the cap,
; so font-size = 10 art px x --zone-px draws caps-1.

